@* <details> and <summary>. No compiler, no state to lose across a fragment
   swap, and it works with scripting off. Giving every item the same Name makes the group
   single-open — shadcn's type="single", straight from the platform. *@
<Accordion Class="w-[480px]">
    <AccordionItem Name="faq" Open>
        <AccordionTrigger>Does it work without JavaScript?</AccordionTrigger>
        <AccordionContent>
            This one does. Anything built on a native element — accordion, dialog, select,
            checkbox — keeps working; the compiler-backed components degrade to plain controls.
        </AccordionContent>
    </AccordionItem>
    <AccordionItem Name="faq">
        <AccordionTrigger>Is the markup really shadcn's?</AccordionTrigger>
        <AccordionContent>
            The class lists are generated from shadcn's own source and compared against it by the
            test suite. Every difference is in deviations.json with a reason.
        </AccordionContent>
    </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>
